{"reference":"1 Samuel 19","book":"1 Samuel","chapter":19,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A difficult description of Saul","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter explicitly says that an evil spirit from the LORD came upon Saul before he again tried to kill David. The wording should not be reduced to a single modern diagnosis: medical, psychological, spiritual, and theological explanations raise distinct questions here.","verse_refs":["1 Samuel 19:9-10"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_samuel_019_6c340081cc9ec1b867aee284"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Within First Samuel","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"This episode stands within First Samuel's larger movement from Eli's failing priestly house, through Samuel's prophetic leadership and Saul's rejected kingship, to David's anointing, rise, exile, and Saul's death. Saul's repeated attempts to seize David in this chapter belong to that wider unfolding account.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_samuel_019_a301fb14110080409362d466"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}